Dear Hiring Team,

#v(0.9em)

I am writing to apply for the *IT Support Specialist (Tier 1)* position in
Buenos Aires. I am studying for my *University Technician Degree in Software
Development* at UADE (current GPA: 8.67) and I am looking for my *first formal
job in IT*. I want to be upfront: I haven't held an IT support title before.
What I do have is hands-on experience solving technical problems for real
users, and I learn tools quickly when someone shows me the right path.

I work with *Windows* and *Linux* every day. I have set up and repaired
desktop computers, laptops, printers and peripherals, and I have supported
non-technical users while they were in the middle of their shift. At Havanna I
maintained the internal systems used by the waiters and validated the data
that went into them. At COTO Digital I log incidents, track requests and fix
printer and device issues so the operation does not stop. That is first-line
support, with people waiting.

I also build software, which helps me troubleshoot beyond the surface. My own
project is a SaaS platform for retail businesses: *Python*, *FastAPI*,
*PostgreSQL*, *Docker* and end-to-end tests with *Playwright*. I am used to
reading logs, reproducing a failure and writing down the steps so it can be
fixed once.

I haven't worked with macOS, Jamf, Intune or Jira yet. I'm comfortable on
Windows and Linux, and I'm willing to learn the Apple and MDM side, which is
the main gap in my background. I'd rather tell you that now than pretend
otherwise.

I'm available to start immediately and to work on-site in Buenos Aires. I'd
be glad to interview at your earliest convenience. Thank you for
considering my application.

Best regards,

#v(1.6em)

*Facundo Octavio Mello*

